      {
        "label": "example-testing",
        "text": "Controlled experiments could help here. If the factory could manipulate their actions and see if the yields decrease, that would provide strong evidence. But in reality, they can't control their actions, so natural experiments might be better. For example, if there was a natural experiment where the factory's actions were followed by a yield decrease, that would support their claim."
