      },
      {
        "label": "deduction",
        "text": "Alternative transportation could be implemented by providing bike lanes or walking trails in the downtown."
      },
      {
        "label": "deduction",
        "text": "Maybe even integrating public transport with walking or cycling services, like a walking bus or a bike-sharing program."
      },
      {
        "label": "deduction",
        "text": "To measure success, the city could track traffic congestion using traffic counters, monitor parking demand, and assess public transport usage."
      },
      {
        "label": "deduction",
        "text": "If these metrics show that congestion is decreasing and public transport is more efficient, the strategy is working."
      },
      {
        "label": "deduction",
        "text": "If not, the strategy might need to be adjusted."
      },
      {
        "label": "deduction",
        "text": "Adapting the strategy over time would involve regularly reviewing the effectiveness of each part of the strategy."
      },
      {
        "label": "example-testing",
        "text": "If, for example, the free parking strategy isn't working, the city could consider other options, like offering free parking during off-peak hours or implementing a more flexible system."
      },
