        "text": "Now, let's check D4 using this recurrence:\n\nD4 should be (16/3)*D3 - 1/3 = (16/3)*(-59) - 1/3 = (-944/3) - 1/3 = (-945)/3 = -315\n\nBut wait, the given determinant for Matrix 4 is -349, not -315."
      },
      {
        "label": "deduction",
        "text": "So, this recurrence doesn't hold for D4."
      },
      {
        "label": "uncertainty-estimation",
        "text": "Hmm, so maybe it's not a linear recurrence of order 1."
      },
      {
        "label": "backtracking",
        "text": "Alternatively, perhaps it's a second-order linear recurrence. Let me assume D_n = a*D_{n-1} + b*D_{n-2}"
      }
    ],
