        "label": "deduction",
        "text": "The sector is a flat part of the cone's surface, so the straight line on the sector will correspond to the path of the rope when it's unwrapped. So, I need to figure out where the starting point and the ending point are on the sector."
      },
      {
        "label": "deduction",
        "text": "The starting point is on the edge of the base of the cone. When we unfold the cone, the base becomes a sector with radius equal to the slant height, which is 2*sqrt(13). The circumference of the base is 8*pi, which we've already used to find the angle of the sector."
      },
      {
        "label": "uncertainty-estimation",
        "text": "So, the starting point is somewhere on the arc of the sector. But where exactly?"
      },
      {
        "label": "deduction",
        "text": "Since the rope is wrapped around the cone starting from a point on the edge of the base, when we unfold the cone, this point will be at a certain position on the arc. Similarly, the apex of the cone is the tip of the sector. So, the straight line on the sector will connect the starting point on the arc to the apex."
      },
      {
        "label": "uncertainty-estimation",
        "text": "But wait, the apex is a single point, so how does the straight line connect? Hmm, maybe I need to think about the parametrization of the cone."
      },
      {
        "label": "backtracking",
