    "chain_full": "To begin, the spiral starts with the number 5 at the center. The subsequent numbers are 8, 11, 14, 17, 20, 23, 26, 29, and 32. However, every third number is replaced by the sum of the two preceding numbers.\n\nThe first three numbers (5, 8, 11) are regular, with 8 being the sum of 5 and 11. The next three (14, 17, 20) are regular, with 17 being the sum of 14 and 17. The third set (23, 26, 29) is regular, with 29 being the sum of 23 and 26. The fourth set (32, ...) will be replaced by the sum of 32 and the next number.\n\nThus, the 15th number is 32, and the 16th number is the sum of 32 and the next number, which is 32 + 32 = 64.\n</think>\n\n**Solution:**\n\n1. **Starting Point:**\n   - The spiral begins with the number 5 at the center.\n   - Subsequent numbers are 8, 11, 14, 17, 20, 23, 26, 29, 32.\n\n2. **Replacement Rule:**\n   - Every third number is replaced by the sum of the two preceding numbers.\n\n3. **Identifying Replacements:**\n   - **3rd number (14):** Sum of 5 and 11.\n   - **6th number (23):** Sum of 23 (already present) and 26.\n   - **9th number (32):** Sum of 32 and the next number (32).\n\n4. **Positions:**\n   - **15th number:** 32\n   - **16th number:** Sum of 32 and the next number (32 + 32 = 64)\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{15\\text{th} = 32,\\quad 16\\text{th} = 64}\n\\]",
