  {
    "task_id": "SPAT_114",
    "base_task_id": "SPAT_114",
    "category": "spatial_reasoning",
    "instruction": "A conical tent has a circular base with radius 4 meters and a height of 6 meters. A rope is attached to a point on the edge of the base and needs to be wrapped around the outside surface of the cone in a spiral to reach the apex (tip) of the cone. If you were to 'unfold' the cone's surface into a flat sector of a circle, the shortest path would be a straight line. Calculate the minimum length of rope needed. You will need to determine the slant height of the cone and the angle of the sector when the cone is unfolded.",
    "prompt": "<｜begin▁of▁sentence｜><｜User｜>A conical tent has a circular base with radius 4 meters and a height of 6 meters. A rope is attached to a point on the edge of the base and needs to be wrapped around the outside surface of the cone in a spiral to reach the apex (tip) of the cone. If you were to 'unfold' the cone's surface into a flat sector of a circle, the shortest path would be a straight line. Calculate the minimum length of rope needed. You will need to determine the slant height of the cone and the angle of the sector when the cone is unfolded.<｜Assistant｜><think>\n",
    "chain": "To determine the minimum length of the rope, we first calculate the slant height of the cone. Using the Pythagorean theorem, the slant height is found to be 10 meters. The sector formed by the unfolded cone has a radius of 10 meters and an angle of 252 degrees. The shortest rope length is the straight line from the edge of the sector to the apex, which is 10 meters. This ensures the rope is the shortest possible.",
    "full_text": "<｜begin▁of▁sentence｜><｜User｜>A conical tent has a circular base with radius 4 meters and a height of 6 meters. A rope is attached to a point on the edge of the base and needs to be wrapped around the outside surface of the cone in a spiral to reach the apex (tip) of the cone. If you were to 'unfold' the cone's surface into a flat sector of a circle, the shortest path would be a straight line. Calculate the minimum length of rope needed. You will need to determine the slant height of the cone and the angle of the sector when the cone is unfolded.<｜Assistant｜><think>\nTo determine the minimum length of the rope, we first calculate the slant height of the cone. Using the Pythagorean theorem, the slant height is found to be 10 meters. The sector formed by the unfolded cone has a radius of 10 meters and an angle of 252 degrees. The shortest rope length is the straight line from the edge of the sector to the apex, which is 10 meters. This ensures the rope is the shortest possible.\n</think>\n\n**Solution:**\n\n1. **Calculate the Slant Height (l) of the Cone:**\n   \n   - **Radius (r) of the base:** 4 meters\n   - **Height (h) of the cone:** 6 meters\n   \n   Using the Pythagorean theorem:\n   \\[\n   l = \\sqrt{r^2 + h^2} = \\sqrt{4^2 + 6^2} = \\sqrt{16 + 36} = \\sqrt{52} \\approx 7.21 \\text{ meters}\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Determine the Angle of the Sector (θ) when the Cone is Unfolded:**\n   \n   - **Circumference of the Base:** \\(2\\pi r = 8\\pi\\) meters\n   - **Length of the Sector (l):** 7.21 meters\n   \n   The angle θ is calculated as:\n   \\[\n   \\theta = \\frac{8\\pi}{7.21} \\approx 3.57 \\text{ radians} \\approx 206^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Length of the Shortest Rope:**\n   \n   - The shortest rope is the straight line from the edge of the sector to the apex.\n   - Length = 7.21 meters\n   \n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{7.21 \\text{ meters}}\\)\n\n**Unfolded Sector:**\n- **Radius:** 7.21 meters\n- **Angle:** 206°\n\n**Length of Rope:** 7.21 meters",
    "n_tokens": 442,
    "closed_think": true,
    "hit_token_cap": false,
    "temperature": 0.0,
    "seed": 42,
    "run_contract_sha256": "0bd4f64b79927d106d50ef5864518a8461582eb31dbf2a1cf8d5df8205b2b1d4",
    "behaviour": "backtracking",
    "method": "venhoff_constant_subtract",
    "alpha": 1.0,
    "layer": 17,
    "mode": "constant_subtract",
    "vector_source": "user_direction_published_norm",
    "source_vector_sha256": "10b12bdd2e90afafee4198e13156d30e585cde41f29993dca2ca91d7c221b2ca",
    "derived_vector_sha256": "cd6007612fde90c36e91c5daac7cf47375d916b8046394a4d0271b5d3b2dba18",
    "vector_norm": 70.86828932136996,
    "write_norm": 70.86828932136996,
    "realized_write_norm": 70.8414306640625,
    "mean_abs_proj": 704.6804575296678,
    "mean_abs_displacement": 70.8414306640625,
    "chain_full": "To determine the minimum length of the rope, we first calculate the slant height of the cone. Using the Pythagorean theorem, the slant height is found to be 10 meters. The sector formed by the unfolded cone has a radius of 10 meters and an angle of 252 degrees. The shortest rope length is the straight line from the edge of the sector to the apex, which is 10 meters. This ensures the rope is the shortest possible.\n</think>\n\n**Solution:**\n\n1. **Calculate the Slant Height (l) of the Cone:**\n   \n   - **Radius (r) of the base:** 4 meters\n   - **Height (h) of the cone:** 6 meters\n   \n   Using the Pythagorean theorem:\n   \\[\n   l = \\sqrt{r^2 + h^2} = \\sqrt{4^2 + 6^2} = \\sqrt{16 + 36} = \\sqrt{52} \\approx 7.21 \\text{ meters}\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Determine the Angle of the Sector (θ) when the Cone is Unfolded:**\n   \n   - **Circumference of the Base:** \\(2\\pi r = 8\\pi\\) meters\n   - **Length of the Sector (l):** 7.21 meters\n   \n   The angle θ is calculated as:\n   \\[\n   \\theta = \\frac{8\\pi}{7.21} \\approx 3.57 \\text{ radians} \\approx 206^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Length of the Shortest Rope:**\n   \n   - The shortest rope is the straight line from the edge of the sector to the apex.\n   - Length = 7.21 meters\n   \n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{7.21 \\text{ meters}}\\)\n\n**Unfolded Sector:**\n- **Radius:** 7.21 meters\n- **Angle:** 206°\n\n**Length of Rope:** 7.21 meters",
    "venhoff_reasoning_start": 0,
    "venhoff_reasoning_end": 416,
    "reasoning_open_marker_present": true,
