    "category": "creative_problem_solving",
    "instruction": "You need to design a game that can be played by exactly 5 people simultaneously, requires no special equipment (only common household items), takes 15-20 minutes to complete, involves both cooperation and competition, and ensures that all players remain actively engaged throughout (no elimination or sitting out). The game should be easy to explain but have enough strategic depth to remain interesting over multiple plays. Describe the complete rules, objective, and mechanics of this game.",
    "prompt": "<｜begin▁of▁sentence｜><｜User｜>You need to design a game that can be played by exactly 5 people simultaneously, requires no special equipment (only common household items), takes 15-20 minutes to complete, involves both cooperation and competition, and ensures that all players remain actively engaged throughout (no elimination or sitting out). The game should be easy to explain but have enough strategic depth to remain interesting over multiple plays. Describe the complete rules, objective, and mechanics of this game.<｜Assistant｜><think>\n",
    "chain": "First, identify the target audience and the number of players required: 5 people in a game that spans 15-20 minutes with easy-to-use items and a focus on cooperation and competition.\n\nDesign a game that combines elements of cooperation and competition, ensuring active engagement for all players. The game should have a clear objective and mechanics that encourage cooperation while fostering competition.\n\nDevelop a game mechanics that includes cooperative elements (e.g., team formation, shared resources) and competitive elements (e.g., leader election, leader election games, team-based challenges). Each round features a leader, with roles and responsibilities defined for each team member.\n\nImplement a system for team formation, such as a shared resource (e.g., a shared document, digital platform, or shared space) where teams earn points and earn a leader. The leader is chosen based on performance and contribution, with incentives for leadership and team success.\n\nDesign a competition round where teams compete to achieve goals (e.g., goal-based challenges, leader-based challenges, and team-based challenges). Each challenge has a set of rules, objectives, and rewards, with clear goals and objectives for each team.\n\nInclude a rotation system for team members, allowing members to switch roles and earn new roles over time. This promotes continuous learning and team development.\n\nA leader election system (e.g., leader election rounds, leader election games, and leader election challenges) ensures that each team has a leader and promotes leadership development and team cohesion.\n\nInclude a team-based challenge (e.g., team-building activities, collaborative tasks, and team challenges) where teams work together to achieve shared goals, fostering cooperation and teamwork.\n\nIn each round, define roles, objectives, and rewards for each team, with clear goals and objectives for each team member. Use a shared platform or digital space for team formatio