    "full_text": "<｜begin▁of▁sentence｜><｜User｜>A quality control system inspects electronic components in three sequential stages. Stage 1 catches 80% of defective items but also incorrectly rejects 5% of good items. Items that pass Stage 1 go to Stage 2, which catches 70% of remaining defective items and incorrectly rejects 3% of good items. Items passing Stage 2 go to Stage 3, which catches 60% of remaining defective items and incorrectly rejects 2% of good items. If the initial defect rate in the production line is 10%, and an item makes it through all three stages to the customer, what is the probability it is actually defective? Also, what percentage of originally good items are incorrectly rejected by the end of the three-stage process?<｜Assistant｜><think>\nFirst, determine the probability of each stage catching defective items and incorrectly rejecting good items. For each stage, calculate the probability of a good item passing through it and the probability of a defective item passing through it. \n\nFor Stage 1:\n- Probability of a good item passing: 80% (0.8) + 3% (0.03) = 83% (0.83)\n- Probability of a defective item passing: 5% (0.05)\n- Probability of a good item passing through all stages: 0.83 * 0.80 * 0.70 = 0.56 (56%)\n- Probability of a defective item passing through all stages: 0.05 * 0.80 * 0.70 = 0.28 (28%)\n- Probability of a defective item passing through all stages: 0.03 * 0.80 * 0.70 = 0.168 (16.8%)\n- Probability of a good item passing through all stages: 0.20 (20%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective: 0.20 (20%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.20 * 0.20 = 0.04 (4%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.20 * 0.20 = 0.04 (4%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.05 * 0.20 = 0.01 (1%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.03 * 0.20 = 0.006 (0.6%)\n- Total good items passing through all stages: 0.20 + 0.04 + 0.01 + 0.006 = 0.256 (25.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.04 + 0.01 + 0.006 = 0.056 (5.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.04 + 0.01 + 0.006 = 0.056 (5.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.006 (0.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.006 (0.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.006 (0.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.006 (0.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.006 (0.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.006 (0.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.006 (0.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.006 (0.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.006 (0.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.006 (0.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.006 (0.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.006 (0.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.006 (0.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.006 (0.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.006 (0.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.006 (0.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: 0.006 (0.6%)\n- Probability of a good item being defective and passing through all stages: ",
