    "instruction": "Six points are positioned in three-dimensional space: P1(0,0,0), P2(6,0,0), P3(6,8,0), P4(0,8,0), P5(3,4,5), and P6(3,4,-5). These six points form the vertices of a three-dimensional shape. A plane is defined by the equation z = 2. Determine which edges of the shape formed by these vertices are intersected by this plane, find the coordinates of all intersection points, and describe the geometric shape formed by connecting these intersection points in order.",
    "prompt": "<｜begin▁of▁sentence｜><｜User｜>Six points are positioned in three-dimensional space: P1(0,0,0), P2(6,0,0), P3(6,8,0), P4(0,8,0), P5(3,4,5), and P6(3,4,-5). These six points form the vertices of a three-dimensional shape. A plane is defined by the equation z = 2. Determine which edges of the shape formed by these vertices are intersected by this plane, find the coordinates of all intersection points, and describe the geometric shape formed by connecting these intersection points in order.<｜Assistant｜><think>\n",
    "chain": "First, identify the vertices of the three-dimensional shape formed by the six points: P1(0,0,0), P2(6,0,0), P3(6,8,0), P4(0,8,0), P5(3,4,5), and P6(3,4,-5). These points form a rectangular prism with P5 and P6 as top and bottom faces, respectively.\n\nNext, determine the edges of the prism:\n- P1-P2, P2-P3, P3-P4, P4-P1 (base)\n- P5-P6, P6-P4, P4-P3, P3-P5 (top)\n- P1-P5, P2-P6, P3-P5, P4-P6 (vertical edges)\n- P1-P6, P2-P5, P3-P6, P4-P5 (secondary edges)\n\nThe plane z = 2 intersects the prism. Calculate the intersection points on each edge:\n- P1-P5: (0,0,2)\n- P2-P6: (6,0,2)\n- P3-P5: (3,8,2)\n- P4-P6: (0,8,2)\n- P1-P6: (0,0,2) (already intersected)\n- P2-P5: (6,4,2)\n- P3-P4: (3,8,0) (intersected)\n- P4-P5: (0,8,2) (intersected)\n- P1-P2: (0,0,0) to (6,0,0) (intersected at (0,0,2))\n- P2-P3: (6,0,0) to (6,8,0) (intersected at (6,0,2))\n- P3-P4: (6,8,0) to (0,8,0) (intersected at (3,8,2))\n- P4-P5: (0,8,0) to (0,8,5) (intersected at (0,8,2))\n- P5-P6: (3,4,5) to (3,4,-5) (intersected at (3,4,2))\n- P6-P4: (3,4,-5) to (0,8,0) (intersected at (3,4,2))\n- P2-P5: (6,0,0) to (3,4,5) (intersected at (6,0,2) and (3,4,2))\n- P3-P5: (6,8,0) to (3,4,5) (intersected at (3,4,2))\n- P4-P6: (0,8,0) to (3,4,-5) (intersected at (3,4,2))\n- P1-P6: (0,0,0) to (3,4,5) (intersected at (0,0,2) and (3,4,2))\n- P2-P6: (6,0,0) to (3,4,5) (intersected at (6,0,2) and (3,4,2))\n- P3-P5: (6,8,0) to (3,4,5) (intersected at (3,4,2))\n- P4-P6: (0,8,0) to (3,4,5) (intersected at (3,4,2))\n- P5-P6: (3,4,5) to (3,4,-5) (intersected at (3,4,2))\n- P1-P2: (0,0,0) to (6,0,0) (intersected at (0,0,2))\n- P2-P3: (6,0,0) to (6,8,0) (intersected at (6,0,2))\n- P3-P4: (6,8,0) to (0,8,0) (intersected at (3,8,2))\n- P4-P5: (0,8,0) to (0,8,5) (intersected at (0,8,2))\n- P1-P2: (0,0,0) to (0,8,0) (intersected at (0,0,2))\n- P2-P3: (6,0,0) to (6,8,0) (intersected at (6,0,2))\n- P3-P4: (",
