) and the expansion of grassland areas. \n15. **Herbicide Use:** The removal of wolves increases the use of herbicides (e.g., grasses, herbicides, and grasses) to manage vegetation and improve water quality. \n16. **Grassland Growth:** The removal of wolves leads to the growth of grassland (e.g., cattails, grasses, and herbaceous plants) and the expansion of grassland areas. \n17. **Herbivores:** The removal of wolves increases the population of herbivores (e.g., catties, deer, and grasses) and the expansion of the food web. \n18.",
