  {
    "task_id": "PROB_115",
    "base_task_id": "PROB_115",
    "category": "probabilistic_thinking",
    "instruction": "A research institute is studying the migration patterns of a rare bird species. Based on historical data, 25% of tagged birds migrate to Region A, 40% migrate to Region B, and 35% migrate to Region C. However, tracking devices have different battery life success rates: devices on birds going to Region A work for the full season 90% of the time, devices on birds going to Region B work 75% of the time, and devices on birds going to Region C work 80% of the time. At the end of the migration season, researchers receive complete tracking data from a randomly selected device. What is the probability that this bird migrated to Region B? Additionally, if the institute tagged 200 birds at the start of the season, how many birds would you expect to have complete tracking data, and among those with complete data, what is the expected distribution across the three regions?",
    "prompt": "<｜begin▁of▁sentence｜><｜User｜>A research institute is studying the migration patterns of a rare bird species. Based on historical data, 25% of tagged birds migrate to Region A, 40% migrate to Region B, and 35% migrate to Region C. However, tracking devices have different battery life success rates: devices on birds going to Region A work for the full season 90% of the time, devices on birds going to Region B work 75% of the time, and devices on birds going to Region C work 80% of the time. At the end of the migration season, researchers receive complete tracking data from a randomly selected device. What is the probability that this bird migrated to Region B? Additionally, if the institute tagged 200 birds at the start of the season, how many birds would you expect to have complete tracking data, and among those with complete data, what is the expected distribution across the three regions?<｜Assistant｜><think>\n",
