    "instruction": "A veterinary researcher observes that domesticated rabbits living in outdoor hutches develop thicker fur during autumn months, but rabbits of the same breed kept indoors with constant temperature and lighting also show some fur thickening in autumn, though less pronounced. The indoor rabbits have no view of windows or access to natural light cycles. Both groups receive identical nutrition. When indoor rabbits are kept on a reversed light cycle (lights on during night hours, off during day hours), they still show fur thickening in autumn months according to the outdoor calendar, not their artificial light cycle. Formulate hypotheses to explain these observations, design experiments to test your hypotheses, and explain what physiological mechanisms might be involved.",
