gy. So, the set of syntacticians is a subset of the set of phonologists.\n\nWait, that's not correct. Let me think again. The statement is that every linguist who specializes in syntax also has expertise in phonology. So, that is, if someone is a linguist, and if they are a syntactician, then they have expertise in phonology. So, the set of syntacticians is a subset of the set of phonologists.\n\nWait, no, that's not correct",
