    "instruction": "A climate model predicts severe storms based on four independent atmospheric conditions: high humidity (occurs 30% of days), low pressure (occurs 25% of days), high wind shear (occurs 20% of days), and temperature inversion (occurs 15% of days). Historical data shows that when all four conditions are present, severe storms occur 95% of the time. When exactly three conditions are present, storms occur 60% of the time. When exactly two conditions are present, storms occur 25% of the time. When fewer than two conditions are present, storms occur 5% of the time. On a given day, a severe storm occurs. What is the probability that all four atmospheric conditions were present? What is the probability that exactly three conditions were present?",
    "prompt": "<｜begin▁of▁sentence｜><｜User｜>A climate model predicts severe storms based on four independent atmospheric conditions: high humidity (occurs 30% of days), low pressure (occurs 25% of days), high wind shear (occurs 20% of days), and temperature inversion (occurs 15% of days). Historical data shows that when all four conditions are present, severe storms occur 95% of the time. When exactly three conditions are present, storms occur 60% of the time. When exactly two conditions are present, storms occur 25% of the time. When fewer than two conditions are present, storms occur 5% of the time. On a given day, a severe storm occurs. What is the probability that all four atmospheric conditions were present? What is the probability that exactly three conditions were present?<｜Assistant｜><think>\n",
