    "instruction": "A wildlife biologist studying a savanna ecosystem notices that zebra populations have remained stable over a decade, but their average body mass has decreased by 18%. During the same period, lion populations declined by 35%, while hyena populations increased by 50%. Rainfall patterns remained normal, and vegetation surveys show no significant changes in grass quality or quantity. However, camera trap data reveals that hyenas now hunt in larger packs (average 8 individuals vs. 4 previously) and are active during more hours of the day. Design a comprehensive investigation to determine what is causing the decrease in zebra body mass. Your response should include: (1) at least three testable hypotheses that could explain this pattern, (2) specific data you would need to collect to evaluate each hypothesis, (3) predictions for what results would support or refute each hypothesis, (4) potential confounding variables that might complicate your interpretation, and (5) an explanation of which hypothesis you consider most plausible based on the existing observations and why.",
