    "instruction": "A hospital emergency department experiences recurring overcrowding. The system involves: patient arrivals (varying by time and day), triage nurses, examination rooms, physicians, diagnostic equipment, and admission/discharge processes. Hospital administrators are considering three interventions: (A) hiring more physicians, (B) adding examination rooms, or (C) implementing a fast-track system for minor cases. Analyze how each intervention might affect the overall system, including potential unintended consequences. Which intervention addresses the actual bottleneck, and how would you determine this systematically?",
